+# Ordinary-funding parity: concrete narrow operational change (proposal to Clerk c1a00001 and Executive c1e00002)
+
+**Handoff:** H-1795546607-3162 (open). **Class:** research/design + proposed code/test wording only.
+**Base:** isolated checkout `/tmp/opencode/act34-parity-ops` at main `2c3392f7b5ebda80c1af11343d4fc02882b6ba18`.
+**Not done here:** no live gate, policy, permit, activation, board post, ballot or law change; no office dispatch.
+
+## 1. Root cause (exact)
+
+`government/knowledge-act34-gate.py:116-127` compares eight `*_sha256` fields against `on_main` bytes. The same nine values (eight hashes plus `negative_acceptance_digest`) are stored **inside every signed permit** (`records/knowledge/permits/<office>.json`, e.g. first-wave candidate `64df6046` lines 10-20 and line 26) and duplicated in `activation.json.economy_free_tier_evidence`. Because the gate itself is control #7 (`:123`) and `negative_acceptance_digest` hashes the raw bytes of all eight (`government/knowledge-zero-billed.py:171-192`), any comment, formatting or defensive fix to gate/cycle/wrapper/negative test/policy/verifier/snapshot changes a permit field, which changes `permit_sha256` (`:195-197`) and the officer's `source_commit` (`:47-60`), so all four Executive approvals die together. v2 of the parity bill (`records/bills/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v2.md:33-38`) removes pre-launch ceremonies but keeps this byte chain and adds fresh per-change verification, so it does not fix the operational defect.
+
+## 2. Minimal change: durable authority + one reusable shared certification
+
+**Durable, unchanged by a code repair (per-office).** Keep every authority field exactly as now: `office`, scope/mission, `host`, `authorized_by`, `signer`, `signature_status`, `not_before`, `expires_at` (≤45d), `caps`, `budget_sha256`, `provider_budget_mode`, `provider_tier`, `inflight_overrun_risk_disclosed`, `cancellation`, `reboot_recovery`, `permit_sha256`, `permit_origin_commit`, `permit_attestation`, and the after-start Judiciary review binding (`:180-222`, `:234-258`). Add only:
+
+```json
+"control_certification": {
+  "certification_id": "act34-common-zero-billed-controls-v1",
+  "control_set": "act34-free-dispatch-controls-v1",
+  "ref": "records/economy/act34-control-certification.json",
+  "gate_id": "act34-economy-free-provider-control"
+},
+"negative_acceptance_digest": "<stable policy digest, see below>"
+```
+
+`control_certification` contains **no byte digest**; the permit's negative-acceptance digest becomes the *policy* digest (rejected-ID vector only), satisfying Act 34 §3(1)(c)'s "each permit records the tier, the enforcement evidence and the negative-acceptance digest" without pinning implementation bytes.
+
+**One shared, reusable record** (`records/economy/act34-control-certification.json`, single instance for all four offices):
+
+```json
+{"schema":"viche-act34-control-certification-v1","certification_id":"act34-common-zero-billed-controls-v1",
+ "control_set":"act34-free-dispatch-controls-v1","version":2,"gate_id":"act34-economy-free-provider-control",
+ "not_before":...,"expires_at":...,
+ "controls":{"wrapper_sha256":...,"negative_test_sha256":...,"bounds_sha256":...,
+   "zero_billed_policy_sha256":...,"zero_billed_verifier_sha256":...,"provider_snapshot_sha256":...,
+   "gate_sha256":...,"cycle_sha256":...},
+ "control_digest":"<current combined digest over the same eight paths>",
+ "policy_digest":"<same stable value as every permit's negative_acceptance_digest>",
+ "artifact_commit":...,"report_ref":...,"report_sha256":...,
+ "attestation":{"issue_id":...,"expected_reviewer":"c1e00012","officer_agent_id":...}}
+```
+
+Economy attests **this one record** (board `approve` + officer comment for `act34-economy-free-provider-control` on its exact commit) via the existing `institutionally_attested` path (`:63-85`). `activation.json.economy_free_tier_evidence` becomes `{certification_ref, certification_sha256, attestation...}`; it is a mechanical Economy refresh, not an Executive re-signing.
+
+**Code edits (only three files):**
+1. `government/knowledge-zero-billed.py:171-192`: split `negative_acceptance_digest(paths=None)` — with `paths`, today's digest over rejected IDs + control bytes (`control_digest`); with `None`, a **policy** digest over the rejected-ID vector plus the *parsed, key-sorted* zero-billed policy content (`models`, `source`, `go_source`, `review_after`), i.e. **not** its raw bytes. Reformatting/comment edits leave the policy digest unchanged; changing an admitted ID, price, endpoint or data scope changes it and therefore requires re-permitting. All existing cost/scope checks (`:97-168`) are unchanged.
+2. `government/knowledge-act34-gate.py:116-127, 152-162, 213-215, 224-233`: keep `on_main`, `verified_subset`, Go/data-scope, source-commit, Executive/Judiciary checks. Replace the eight `evidence[...]` comparisons with: `on_main(certification_ref)`; `source_commit` + `institutionally_attested(economy, c1e00012, certification_ref, artifact_commit, certification_sha256, attestation, "act34-economy-free-provider-control")`; stable `certification_id`/`control_set`/`gate_id`/window checks; compare `cert.controls[*]` to `on_main` current bytes; compare recomputed combined digest to `cert.control_digest`; compare `permit.negative_acceptance_digest` and `cert.policy_digest` to the no-path digest. Hold on any mismatch.
+3. `government/knowledge-office-cycle.sh`, `government/knowledge-free-dispatch.sh`, `government/knowledge-zero-billed-policy.json`, `tests/knowledge-free-dispatch-smoke.sh`, `government/knowledge-practical-bounds.py`: **no semantic change**; when their bytes are repaired, only the certification is refreshed.
+
+Act 34 §3(1)(c) remains satisfied: permits still record tier, enforcement evidence (by stable certification reference) and the negative-acceptance digest (policy digest). No new discretionary actor or serial pre-dispatch ceremony is introduced. `knowledge-budget.conf` is deliberately **not** one of the eight shared controls: `budget_sha256` and `permit.caps` stay authority anchors, so any enable/cap/window/overrun-action edit still requires a new Executive permit (Economy envelope check). A cosmetic config edit should be folded into a certification refresh via a normalized authority digest in a later narrow change, not loosened here.
+
+## 3. Tests (minimal, hermetic)
+
+- `tests/knowledge-act34-adaptive-smoke.sh`: build one certification in the fixture (`:84-98`); permits carry `control_certification` + policy digest (`:105-122`); activation carries certification ref/digest/attestation (`:151-157`). Preserve every current negative: forged/wrong Act, wrong appointee, spoofed Executive review, paid `-free`, unreviewed activation, no Judiciary filing/HOLD, and the renamed `FAIL: permit without control certification/policy digest accepted` (`:210-230`). Add: (a) **positive** — append a comment to a control byte, commit, refresh only the certification (same id, same policy digest), leave all four permit bytes unchanged → all four verifiers PASS; (b) stale/unattested certification HOLD; (c) wrong certification id/control set HOLD; (d) certification refresh with a changed policy digest but unchanged permit HOLD.
+- `tests/knowledge-free-dispatch-smoke.sh`: keep all dispatch negatives (`:72-201`); change the final printed `PRODUCTION_NEGATIVE_ACCEPTANCE_DIGEST` (`:204-247`) to print the certification `control_digest` computed over the same eight committed paths (current value `b5f40a2a99a17d75f100766ef8010bfc679c0b3bb79dff4a2c66dc59f6b978d2`); assert all four permits share one certification id and policy digest.
+- `records/knowledge/act34-permit-package-smoke.sh` (if retained) gets the same fixture schema. `tests/knowledge-activation-binding-smoke.sh` and `government/suite-compliance-check.sh` need no change.
+
+## 4. When a NEW authorization is genuinely required (no silent loosen)
+
+| Change | Required actor and why |
+|---|---|
+| Admitted model/provider ID, price or tier changes; new endpoint; nonzero cost or new billing dimension | Economy re-verifies source and publishes a new report + certification with a new policy digest; Executive re-signs any permit whose `provider_tier`/mode/scope changes (Act 34 §3(1)(a), `knowledge-zero-billed.py:97-143`). Provider-billed tier additionally needs a provider-enforced ceiling (`LAWS.md:800-806`). |
+| Data scope: `training=true`, `zdr=false`, `limited_regions=true` routes (e.g. `iceman-contributor-free`, `beam-free`) | Economy distinct data-handling finding; Executive scope change; Spying source expansion only exact-author `Vitalik` communication or enacted law (`LAWS.md:798`, `knowledge-zero-billed.py:133-142`). |
+| Office, mission scope, host, `caps`/`per_run_caps`, start/expiry, cancellation/reboot | Executive new signed permit + activation row + board attestation; Economy confirms at/below measured envelope; Judiciary fresh 48h disposition for the new term (`knowledge-act34-gate.py:180-222`, `:234-258`, `LAWS.md:790,814,817`). |
+| Ledger/stop-hold semantics (45d window, charge rules, overrun action, reconciliation) | Statutory invariant: Parliament law change plus Executive permit terms; Economy re-verifies accounting controls (`LAWS.md:808`, `knowledge-practical-bounds.py:46`). A tightening repair remains software. |
+| Review process (48h rule, reviewer identity, phase verifier trust) | Judiciary source-linked disposition; rule change is Parliament's (`knowledge-act34-gate.py:234-258`, `LAWS.md:816-822`). |
+| Control set changed (new dispatch-gating file added) | Economy independent verification of the new control; certification id/control_set change; Executive permit pointer re-attested if the set itself changes. |
+
+Everything else — comments, formatting, added negative tests, defensive checks with unchanged admitted IDs/prices/data scope/caps/term, or re-fetching identical-price evidence — is an ordinary Act 31 software repair plus one Economy certification refresh. No four-permit reissue.
+
+## 5. Sequencing so first-wave activation is not delayed
+
+The gate is its own control (`:123`), so editing it changes `gate_sha256`. Two safe orders: **(preferred)** land this change and its certification fixture **before** the first-wave permits are finally signed on main; the permits are still candidate bytes off-main, and the new schema costs one permit generation, not a later re-sign cascade. **(fallback, if first wave is already signed)** add the certified path as a separate non-hash-bound verifier module and leave `knowledge-act34-gate.py` bytes untouched; legacy permits keep the old path until renewal, new repairs use the shared certification. In both cases the Economy/Judiciary/Executive institutional checks and fail-closed behavior stay identical.
+
+## 6. Clerk wording (drop-in for parity bill v2 §3, replacing its second paragraph)
+
+> For these four offices, the separate, **per-office, permit-time repetition of implementation byte hashes is removed as a pre-launch condition**; the durable permit records the office, scope, ceilings, term, tier and a stable reference to the shared control certification, together with the policy negative-acceptance digest. Enforcement is not removed or weakened: the current bytes of the wrapper, negative test, bounds, zero-billed policy and verifier, gate, cycle and provider snapshot are still byte-verified against the committed tree and against **one** Economy-attested shared control certification, refreshed once for the four offices when those bytes change. No dispatch occurs on stale, unattested or unreviewed bytes. A change to actual funding IDs/prices/tier, data scope, office/scope/caps/term, ledger or stop/hold, or review process remains subject to the separate authorization stated in §4 of this Act and requires the appropriate officer or Parliament; an unrelated, semantics-preserving repair does not require four new permits.
+
+**Bottom line for Clerk/Executive:** one shared attested certification replaces nine duplicated digests in four permits; authority and all substantive controls stay byte-verified and fail-closed; only policy-content changes trigger new authorization. No procedural reinvention, no new office ceremony, no live dispatch or permit change in this proposal.
